# Client transport follow-up

- Recovery after a server restart with the browser online waits on backoff: no browser
  signal says the server is back, so the first connection through depends on the
  retry delay (a Loro room's fixed `RETRY_MS`, at most 10 s and without jitter; the thread
  socket's randomized `persistentDelayMs`, up to 30 s). Peer success then pulls the other
  connections within ~0.5 s. Every room retries on the same schedule, so a restart brings
  them back together; add jitter or lower the caps with production deploy-restart data.
